##RISKS AND BEST PRACTICES
Running an Instagram theme page involves more than just creating content and gaining followers. You also need to protect your account, follow platform policies and avoid practices that could affect your page's long-term growth.



Copyright and Content Ownership - 
When repurposing content from other Instagram pages, YouTube or other platforms, make sure you have the necessary permission or usage rights.

How to do it: 
Prefer original content or content available under a suitable licence.
Contact the original creator if you want to reuse their videos, images or designs.
Obtain permission in writing whenever possible.
Check the usage terms of stock footage, images and music.
Keep records of permissions and licences.
Avoid assuming that giving credit or changing subtitles makes copyrighted content free to use.



Follow Instagram Guidelines - 
Instagram has rules regarding content, account behaviour and monetization. Violating these rules can result in content removal, reduced distribution or account restrictions.

How to do it:
Read Instagram's Community Guidelines.
Avoid posting prohibited or misleading content.
Don't use spam tactics, fake engagement or automated interactions.
Check your account's Account Status regularly.
Review monetization eligibility and content policies before applying for monetization features.



Avoid Fake Engagement - 
Buying followers, likes or views might make your account appear popular, but it does not build a genuine audience.

What to avoid: 
Buying followers or engagement.
Using bots to generate likes and comments.
Participating in artificial engagement groups.
Using suspicious third-party growth services.

Focus on attracting people who are genuinely interested in your niche. 



Adapt to Algorithm Changes - 
Instagram regularly updates how content is recommended and distributed. A strategy that works today might not produce the same results in the future.

How to do it: 
Follow updates from Instagram's official creator channels.
Experiment with different Reel and carousel formats.
Monitor changes in reach and engagement.
Identify which content formats continue to perform well.
Adjust your posting and content strategy based on actual performance.



Maintain Content Quality - 
Posting frequently doesn't necessarily mean your page will grow. Focus on providing content that your audience finds useful, entertaining or interesting. 

Things to follow: 
Maintain consistent editing and visual quality.
Use clear and readable subtitles.
Write relevant captions.
Avoid misleading hooks and clickbait.
Don't sacrifice quality just to meet a posting target.

Secure Your Account - 
Losing access to an established Instagram page can affect your entire business.

How to do it:
Use a strong and unique password.
Enable two-factor authentication.
Add a recovery email and phone number.
Never share OTPs or login credentials.
Avoid suspicious links and unofficial applications.
Review devices and login sessions connected to your account.



Manage Your Finances - 
As your page starts generating revenue, keep track of your income and expenses.

How to do it:
Record all earnings from promotions, affiliate marketing and other sources.
Track expenses such as software subscriptions, freelancers and marketing.
Calculate your actual monthly profit.
Keep records of payments and invoices.
Set aside money for applicable taxes.
Maintain a separate record of business-related transactions.



Important things to remember - 
Audience growth takes time and consistency.
High follower counts don't guarantee high earnings.
Don't depend entirely on Instagram as your only source of income.
Always prioritise account safety and audience trust.
Build a sustainable business rather than chasing short-term viral growth.




